"In his first week Nathan Lark took High-tier Magic Resistance and declined Resolute Mind."
"Years later Nathan held three Talents: Arcane Nullfield, Immortal Body and Airwalking."
"Years later, Airwalking read: \"This Talent will allow you to use Stamina to push off of air\""
"\"with any part of your body. The greater the force exerted, the greater the Stamina required.\""
"Immortal Body read: \"You have achieved precise control of your body at a minuscule level\""
"\"and the ability to reconstitute your body from near-total obliteration with Focus.\""
"\"This Talent will automatically spend Stamina to efficiently and immediately heal wounds.\""
"\"It can also bring you back from the smallest remaining speck of living tissue\""
"\"if you have Focus remaining. You can spend Stamina to make innate changes,\""
"\"which include banishing poison, countering aging, and restructuring your body\""
"\"on a minuscule level. Larger wounds and greater changes will cost more stamina.\""
"\"You can only die via total obliteration or running out of Stamina or Focus.\""
"Nathan's first Talent capped out and drove him to seek a regeneration Talent instead."
"Foresight Talents fail on Nathan; Davrar cannot predict his outcomes."
"Later, Stella held Conduit of Mana, her unique version of the Mana Shaping Talent."
"Later, Garna held a Talent to make ranged weapons appear already in flight."
"Later, Brox held a speed Talent he would not teach."
"Later, Aarl's Talent Spatial Blade let blades grow or shrink slightly as they swung."
"Years later, Khachi's Talent Unwavering Zeal sat at rank ten a long time before it Developed."
"Years later, Khachi's Talent Nascent Divinity Developed into Godhead."
"Years later, Nathan's Immortal Body rose from 7 to 8 after he reshaped his face with it."
